sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P0 as Reader (Guest / signed-in)
    participant P1 as Web Application (News UI)
    participant P2 as EngagementController
    participant P3 as Application Database
    P0->>P1: open article
    P1->>P2: GET /news/{id}/engagement
    P2->>P3: verify active news
    P3-->>P2: return news record
    P2->>P2: create viewer key and session-bound encrypted token
    P2-->>P1: return token, set news_visitor cookie
    Note over P0,P3: The UI waits for the qualified reading interval while the document is visible. Server accepts token age 5 seconds to 2 hours.
    P1->>P2: POST /news/{id}/view (token)
    P2->>P2: decrypt, validate news ID, token age and session
    alt [invalid token]
    P2-->>P1: 422: reject view request
    else [valid token]
    P2->>P3: begin transaction, lock active news
    P2->>P3: check hashed visit ID in news_visits
    P3-->>P2: return visit existence
    alt [visit already recorded]
    P2->>P3: read unchanged unique_views, commit
    else [new visit]
    P2->>P3: insert news_visits, check news_viewers
    P3-->>P2: return viewer existence
    opt [new viewer]
    P2->>P3: insert news_viewers, increment news.unique_views
    end
    P2->>P3: increment news.view, commit
    end
    P3-->>P2: return unique_views
    P2-->>P1: JSON: unique_views
    P1-->>P0: update displayed view count
    end
    Note over P0,P3: Repeat submissions of one visit token do not increment counts again. A new visit from a known viewer increases total views, but not unique views.
